  "LEZ-08-100|A|2026-11-17": {"short":"System record","change":"A 60 lb lead block bolted \"through the nose bulkhead\", drawn as a 44 in³ box (18 lb of lead)."},
  "LEZ-08-100|B|2026-11-18": {"short":"Defined; host bulkhead","change":"60 lb of lead is 146 in³; the nose ahead of the nose-gear box holds about 102 in³ above WL 33 (landing light and nose-gear parts below). As defined: a forward block cast to the nose contour (41.76 lb gross) and two side slabs aft of the new nose ballast bulkhead LEZ-08-105 (FS 6.87), clamped by 4 × AN5-62A between 0.125 in 4130 plates; lines through it get short straight holes. Centroid FS 5.96 (was 5.52). Check ballast-bolt; the bulkhead takes ballast-bhd."},
  "LEZ-08-100|C|2026-11-19": {"short":"Steel density 0.283","change":"Laminate values from the sources: 7715 UNI 7.30 oz/yd², cured 0.0094 in at v_f 0.417, E1 33.5 GPa; 7725 BID 8.80 oz/yd², cured 0.0113 in; H45 and Styrofoam at their published minimums; hot-wet fc 0.70 / fs 0.48 (NCAMP 7781); post-cure 15 h at 80 °C in the oven (MGS L285 powered-aircraft schedule, oven size not a constraint). Faces and hard points are thicker by the cured ply (0.0113 in); the solid is rebuilt; checks hold the reserve; 4130 at 0.283 lb/in³."},
  "LEZ-08-105|A|2026-11-18": {"short":"Initial definition","change":"New part (coordinator M-17): the fixed ballast had no host (\"through the nose bulkhead\"; none existed) and its inserts were in mid-air. A 0.436 in PVC sandwich at FS 6.87, just ahead of the nose-gear box, with solid-BID hard points where the side slabs bear; every ballast piece bears on it in a forward crash (ballast-bhd)."},
  "LEZ-08-105|C|2026-11-19": {"short":"Holes from the swept footprint","change":"Pass-through holes sized from each line's swept footprint through the whole thickness (the tube at both faces and between, its radius and clearance), not from the mid-plane crossing alone, and built after every parts module has loaded (lines re-routed later are in the table); the forward harness, which ran 0.58 in into the laminate with no hole, gets one. New check ballast-slab."},
