  "LEZ-08-110|E|2026-11-19": {"short":"MTM45-1 prepreg conversion (block P); re-sized","change":"Plates 10 → 11.5 lb each: the prepreg airframe's empty CG is further aft, and with two 10 lb plates the lightest pilot the placard could take was 126 lb (R-INT-2 asks ≤ 125); with 11.5 lb plates it is 118 lb. 11.5 lb is the most the slab plates take before the lead reaches block E's NG-30 plate cap at FS 10.15 (lead now ends FS 10.13); pins re-checked. Laminate system: MTM45-1 prepreg (NCAMP), M cycle (Miles, 2026-11-19): MTM45-1 / 6781 S2-glass fabric (0.0101 in cured) for skins, webs, faces and the glass caps (laid 0/90), MTM45-1 / HTS40 carbon unitape (0.0055 in) for the wing, canard, CS-spar and jut-out caps, Divinycell HT61 cores CNC-milled (the lowest density that passes), FM 300-2 for core and secondary bonds. Allowables NCAMP MH × 0.72 (6781, HTS40: mean × 0.8 × 0.9) at ETW 200 °F, BOUND until the M-cycle coupon programme (DOT/FAA/AR-03/19); cure 250 ± 10 °F for 4–6 h, ≥ 28 inHg, no post-cure; out-time ≤ 10 days, storage ≤ 0 °F. CNC core programme in place of the hot-wire templates; the steps read debulk, bag, cure."},
  "LEZ-20-100|A|2026-11-19": {"short":"Initial definition","change":"Initial definition. Mass was ASSUMED (0.006 lb a clamp). Now the hardware lines by dash size with clamp, screw, nutplate and standoff. The right raceway clamp at FS 87.6 now sits at BL ≥ 10.5 (B's ask); LP is at WL 35.04, LS at WL 37.44."},
  "LEZ-20-100|B|2026-11-19": {"short":"Aft-lane conduit; brake-line span","change":"Option A (Miles): the aft systems lane's nylon conduit (both sides: CS spar low tunnel, jut-out lane, wing panels) and the GMU 11 side-port grommet are hardware lines here, with their mass (nylon density typed). A clamp slid off a bulkhead plane no longer leaves a span over the rule: an extra clamp goes into that span (block D's brake lines at the panel, 9.73 in against 9 in; R-ROUTE-1)."},
  "LEZ-20-100|C|2026-11-19": {"short":"Conduit rule sources; grommet swap","change":"Source audit (2026-11-19): the 40 % fill rule is cited to NEC Ch. 9 Table 1 and the AC 43.13-1B para 11-249 ID ≥ 1.25 × bundle check is added (I4); nylon 0.0383 and phenolic 0.0484 lb/in³ (sourced); the left spar-web grommet is an MS35489-11 (3/8 ID, 5/8 hole), which passes the 3/8 liner (the -7 is 1/4 ID and cannot): A to open the web hole (ICD ask). The 1/2 × 0.035 nylon tube is not a stock Nylaflow size (BOUND; see the docs)."},
  "LEZ-20-100|D|2026-11-19": {"short":"Aft conduit 6061-T6 1/2 × 0.035","change":"ICD A-S3: the aft-lane conduit is stock 6061-T6 drawn tube 1/2 × 0.035 (ID 0.430; Aircraft Spruce 03-35800, 0.0612 lb/ft): GMU harness fill 34 % ≤ 40 %, ID / bundle 1.72 ≥ 1.25 (AC 43.13-1B 11-249). Left power raceway 0.12 in lower (elec-emc +0.13)."},
  "LEZ-20-110|A|2026-11-19": {"short":"Initial definition","change":"Initial definition. Mass was ASSUMED; now the hardware lines (clamp, screw, bonded G-10 tab)."},
